Modifications by the claude-code-proxy-rs project include application naming,
browser storage namespaces, local development configuration and verification,
removal of OpenAI/xAI upstream implementations and product entry points,
management-only startup, shared TLS trust configuration, Claude API Key account
management, provider-aware credential rotation, and bounded model-catalog
connectivity checks, native Anthropic Messages JSON/SSE forwarding, bounded
usage observation, execution deadlines, and Claude Code configuration export
with the corresponding frontend and HTTP acceptance tests.
Subsequent changes replace API Key onboarding with Claude Code OAuth/Setup Token,
PKCE authorization, refresh scheduling, proxy-only Bearer transport, and the
corresponding account management UI and isolated HTTP acceptance tests.
Further changes add unified Claude client identity configuration, per-account
overrides, locally captured TLS templates, HTTPS proxy transport, and regression tests.
The backend workspace and frontend design originate from the upstream project.
Original third-party package names and provider protocol identifiers are retained.

The frontend consumes @codex-proxy/ui from zyycn/codex-proxy-ui under its own
license. Package provenance and the fixed revision are recorded in the lockfile.
The sub2api project is a design reference; no sub2api source is included here.
